title: The Coalition Council
subtitle: Every unresolved bargain has found its way into the same room.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_government_card
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and ministries_finalized = 1 and ministry_count >= 1 and month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_coalition_council_timer <= 0 and government_coalition_dissent >= 6
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_coalition_council_timer = 4
card-image: img/poland/cards/government-affairs.webp

= The Coalition Council

[? if government_party = "pis": Kaczyński arrives with the votes counted and
the senior ministries already marked **not negotiable**. Morawiecki wants the
social side of the agreement to produce visible results; Ziobro wants every
concession to Lewica described as surrender. Our ministers have deadlines of
their own, and Razem is waiting outside the room to explain what we traded
away.?]
[? if government_party != "pis": Parties outside the cabinet do not acquire a
seat in this room by being historically familiar. Lewica's ministers have
deadlines of their own.?]
[? if government_party != "pis" and (ministry_ko_in_cabinet = 1 or
government_party = "ko"): KO has a veto list.?]
[? if government_party != "pis" and (ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or
government_party = "psl"): PSL has several red lines.?]
[? if government_party != "pis" and (ministry_p2050_in_cabinet = 1 or
government_party = "p2050"): Poland 2050 has circulated a diagram.?]
[? if government_party != "pis": The council can concentrate on shared
delivery, exchange priorities or let the public see where agreement ends.?]

- @delivery_cell
- @exchange_deadlines
- @publish_minutes
- @leave_pis_cabinet

@delivery_cell
title: Staff a joint delivery cell
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Move disputes from leaders' offices into accountable work.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A joint delivery team requires one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; government_coalition_dissent -= 6; ko_coalition_dissent -= 2 if ministry_ko_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "ko"; psl_coalition_dissent -= 2 if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "psl"; p2050_coalition_dissent -= 2 if ministry_p2050_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "p2050"; pis_relation += 2 if government_party = "pis"; government_delivery += 3; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The coalition creates a joint delivery cell with published deadlines"

Officials receive named decisions, deadlines and escalation rules. The council
does not become friendlier, but it loses the ability to rediscover the same
disagreement every fortnight.

- #poland_card_finish


@exchange_deadlines
title: Exchange one Left deadline for one coalition concession
subtitle: Reduce cabinet tension by narrowing the immediate programme.
on-arrival: government_coalition_dissent -= 5; ko_relation += 2 if ministry_ko_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "ko"; psl_relation += 2 if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "psl"; p2050_relation += 2 if ministry_p2050_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "p2050"; pis_relation += 3 if government_party = "pis"; progressive_credibility -= 2; progressives_dissent += 4; government_delivery += 1; news_headline = "Coalition leaders trade deadlines and recover a working calendar"

One reform moves back and one material commitment moves forward. Ministers
leave with a calendar they can pass; activists leave with another reason to
ask whether governability always sends them the invoice.

- #poland_card_finish


@publish_minutes
title: Publish the disagreements and keep negotiating
subtitle: No resource or budget cost. Transparency is not harmony, but it is a floor.
on-arrival: public_trust += 3; constitutional_restraint += 2; party_unity += 1; government_coalition_dissent -= 1; ko_coalition_dissent += 1 if ministry_ko_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "ko"; psl_coalition_dissent += 1 if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "psl"; p2050_coalition_dissent += 1 if ministry_p2050_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "p2050"; pis_relation -= 2 if government_party = "pis"; news_headline = "The coalition publishes its unresolved disputes instead of staging unanimity"

The minutes distinguish blocked policy from unfinished administration and
name which partner objects. The atmosphere worsens for an afternoon and the
public record improves for longer.

- #poland_card_finish


@leave_pis_cabinet
title: Withdraw every Lewica minister
subtitle: End the coalition, lose cabinet authority and leave Morawiecki to govern as a PiS minority.
view-if: government_party = "pis"
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const portfolios = [
    "labor", "equality", "housing", "health", "digital", "science",
    "interior", "finance", "economy", "justice", "foreign",
    "agriculture", "defence"
];
const fallbackPiSMinisters = {
    labor: "Marlena Maląg",
    equality: "Anna Schmidt",
    housing: "Piotr Uściński",
    health: "Adam Niedzielski",
    digital: "Janusz Cieszyński",
    science: "Przemysław Czarnek",
    interior: "Mariusz Kamiński",
    finance: "Tadeusz Kościński",
    economy: "Piotr Nowak",
    justice: "Zbigniew Ziobro",
    foreign: "Zbigniew Rau",
    agriculture: "Grzegorz Puda",
    defence: "Mariusz Błaszczak"
};
for (const portfolio of portfolios) {
    if (Q[portfolio + "_minister_party"] == "Lewica") {
        const savedDefault = String(
            Q["ministry_" + portfolio + "_default_minister"] || ""
        );
        Q[portfolio + "_minister_party"] =
            Q["ministry_" + portfolio + "_default_party"] || "PiS";
        Q[portfolio + "_minister"] =
            savedDefault &&
            !/nominee|unassigned|development ministry/i.test(savedDefault)
                ? savedDefault
                : fallbackPiSMinisters[portfolio];
    }
}
Q.family_minister_party = Q.labor_minister_party;
Q.family_minister = Q.labor_minister;
Q.left_in_government = 0;
Q.left_cabinet_committed = 0;
Q.left_cabinet_model = "Parliamentary opposition";
Q.razem_in_government = 0;
Q.razem_government_role = "Lewica opposition caucus";
Q.position = "Parliamentary opposition";
Q.left_role = "Opposition after withdrawing from Morawiecki's cabinet";
Q.government_name = "Third Morawiecki Cabinet — PiS minority";
Q.government_owner = "PiS minority government";
Q.coalition_status = "PiS minority after New Left withdrawal";
Q.coalition_seats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.pis_seats) || 0);
Q.government_support_seats = Q.coalition_seats;
Q.ministry_count = 0;
Q.ministry_left_cabinet_seats = 0;
Q.ministries_finalized = 1;
Q.cabinet_roster_government_party = "pis";
Q.budget = 0;
Q.budget_authority = "Opposition — no state spending authority";
Q.pis_relation -= 18;
Q.ko_relation += 8;
Q.p2050_relation += 5;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 15;
Q.progressive_credibility += 5;
Q.news_headline =
    "New Left ministers resign and Morawiecki loses his majority";
!}

= The nameplates come down

Our ministers submit their resignations together. PiS deputies call it
desertion; Razem asks why it took this long; KO offers no absolution for the
months in which our votes sustained the cabinet. By nightfall the civil
servants report to PiS nominees again and Morawiecki is back to counting every
bill.

Leaving restores the freedom to oppose. It does not erase the record of having
governed.

- #poland_card_finish
